From 8cc17e3cd5121b099a8181cba806b78c45468456 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 14:23:54 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] kcm_pulseaudio: Sound page: devices first, app streams built
 after them, toolbar actions become links, module options on a sub-page
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Device-style list of output and input devices (peers), then apps. PulseAudio/PipeWire models, kcfg
(GlobalConfig), speaker/microphone tests and module settings behaviour unchanged. NOT BUILT YET (owner stopped heavy
work); checked statically only.

Moved / renamed:
- Toolbar (Show Inactive Devices switch, Rename Devices…, Configure Volume Controls…, Configure… menu) is gone. A link
  row now ends the output section: "Show inactive devices" checkbox, "Volume Controls…", "Rename Devices…" (PipeWire +
  WirePlumber only, as before), "Output Behavior…" (PulseAudio only, as before: Server.isPipeWire false).
- "Configure…" menu (two checkable actions) -> new sub-page ui/OutputBehavior.qml, a FormLayout with the same two texts;
  disabled with a "Requires module-gsettings PulseAudio module" hint when the module is not loaded (was the toolbar tooltip).
- Section titles: Playback Devices -> Output Devices, Recording Devices -> Input Devices, Inactive Cards -> Unused Sound
  Cards, Playback Streams -> Apps Playing Sound, Recording Streams -> Apps Recording Sound (user words; old names go to
  the page aliases in ia/layout.json).
- The device rows (default radio + volume first, then Port/Profile/Test/Show Channels) are unchanged; a per-device
  sub-page was not attempted without a build.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006, HIG-023, HIG-057; page-design.md 1, 2, 4, 6, 7.

Speed cause (code evidence): the first frame built ModuleManager (3 GSettingsItem objects, g_settings schema lookups and
a module scan: modulemanager.cpp ctor) although it is PulseAudio-only and only used by a menu; now created on its
sub-page only. The streams (StreamRestoreModel, SinkInputModel, SourceOutputModel and their level-meter delegates) sat in
the same ColumnLayout as the devices; they now sit in a Loader { asynchronous: true } built after the device lists. No
sync D-Bus exists in src/kcm. The two OverlaySheets (speaker/microphone test) are still created up front; making them lazy
needs the testSink()/testSource() ids reworked, not done. After-numbers: pending, manager will measure. Not built yet.
Unconfirmed: Loader inside ColumnLayout taking its height from the async-loaded ColumnLayout (width bound to parent.width);
ids sinkInputView/eventStreamView resolving from StreamListItem inside the Component; Flow with Layout.fillWidth.
inventory_check --strict lists 13 unchanged weak-anchor rows in files not touched (DeviceListItem etc.); non-strict is 0 lost.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
